WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:05.000
Run multiple Valheim worlds in one place, each with its own mods and settings.

00:00:05.000 --> 00:00:10.000
One Docker container. A setup wizard. Multiple vanilla and modded Valheim worlds.

00:00:10.000 --> 00:00:15.000
Manage multiple worlds from your browser: start, stop, update, settings and logs.

00:00:15.000 --> 00:00:20.000
Choose vanilla or modded, crossplay, passwords, server listing and launch parameters for each world. Consoles cannot load mods.

00:00:20.000 --> 00:00:25.000
Set each world’s update window, quiet period, timeout and backup-first policy. Player-aware updates require Companion telemetry.

00:00:25.000 --> 00:00:30.000
Select mods from Thunderstore, Hexium or Hugin's Vibes. Pin versions or follow the latest.

00:00:30.000 --> 00:00:35.000
Edit mod settings in the browser. Saved overrides are reapplied when the world starts or updates.

00:00:35.000 --> 00:00:40.000
Resolve dependencies and package each world’s mods and shared configurations for players. Server-only configs stay private.

00:00:40.000 --> 00:00:45.000
Pick a world. The PhValheim client syncs mods and settings before launch. Vanilla worlds use ordinary Valheim.

00:00:45.000 --> 00:00:50.000
Choose per-world backup schedules and retention, manage access lists, admins and bans, and inspect logs.

00:00:50.000 --> 00:00:55.000
Ask Hugin for help. Build and package mods in Vibes; publish locally and try them on test worlds. AI optional.

00:00:55.000 --> 00:01:00.000
More worlds. Less admin. Host, configure, mod, sync and play. Get started at phvalheim.com.
